nmental chemistry and pollution control</li><li>Renewable energy and circular economy</li></ul>\n<h3>5. Health Sciences and Biotechnology</h3>\n<ul><li>Public health innovations and policy</li><li>Biotechnology and biomedical research</li><li>Environmental and occupational health</li><li>One Health approaches</li></ul>\n<h3>6. Education, Pedagogy and Curriculum Innovation</h3>\n<ul><li>STEM education and competency-based education</li><li>Digital learning and educational technologies</li><li>Quality assurance and higher education reforms</li><li>Research supervision and postgraduate training</li></ul>\n<h3>7. Governance, Leadership and Socio-Economic Development</h3>\n<ul><li>Public policy and governance</li><li>Entrepreneurship, MSMEs and innovation-driven growth</li><li>Gender, equity and social inclusion</li><li>Community engagement and sustainable livelihoods</li></ul>\n<h3>8. Interdisciplinary Research and Industry–Academia Collaboration</h3>\n<ul><li>Cross-disciplinary research approaches</li><li>University–industry partnerships</li><li>Research-to-policy and research-to-practice pathways</li></ul>\n\n<h2>Important Dates</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Milestone</th><th>Date</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Call for Abstracts/Exhibitions Opens</td><td>July 13, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Deadline for Abstract Submission</td><td>August 31, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Notification of Abstract Acceptance</td><td>Rolling (as received)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Early Bird Registration Deadline</td><td>September 18, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Deadline for Registration &amp; Payment</td><td>September 30, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Conference/Exhibition Dates</td><td>October 21–23, 2026</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2>Registration Fees</h2>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Fee</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Research paper oral/poster presentation</td><td>KES 3,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Exhibition fees</td><td>KES 10,000</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Exhibition fees for high schools<